# phi-agent — A1 (assistant) perimeter (phios-agente.md §4.3).
#
# Recomputed per active project: no other project is visible (§4.3). The
# active project name comes from PHI_AGENT_PROJECT; when it is unset the
# @PROJECT@ lines below expand to an empty path and are skipped by the "?"
# suffix, so the container still starts for the V-01..V-04 proof without a
# project selected. S-73 populates the real §8.2 tree and `phi agent
# project` writes PHI_AGENT_PROJECT.
#
# Ordering: the project is bound read-only first; proposte/ and output/ are
# re-bound writable underneath it afterwards. memoria.md, materiali/ and
# archivio/ therefore stay read-only. The explicit memoria.md line below is
# the visible form of the §8.4 / ADR 094 guarantee: the agent CANNOT write
# its own memory, and that is enforced by this mount, not by the interface.
# Only `phi agent memory accept` (the client, outside the containment)
# promotes a proposte/ file into memoria.md.

# A1's own XDG trees — writable (§4.3 "albero XDG di A1: scrittura").
# opencode keeps its sessions, auth and cache here.
rw   @AGENT_DATA@                @CONTAINER_HOME@/.local/share
rw   @AGENT_STATE@               @CONTAINER_HOME@/.local/state
rw   @AGENT_CACHE@               @CONTAINER_HOME@/.cache

# The engine config, read-only. A single file, not the whole .config dir.
# "?" — you create it from opencode.example.json (it carries the model id,
# §6). Absent, opencode cannot start, but a bare `sh` in the container
# still can, so the V-01..V-04 proof runs before any provider setup.
ro?  @AGENT_CONFIG@/opencode/opencode.json   @CONTAINER_HOME@/.config/opencode/opencode.json

# Personalities — read-only (§4.3). "personalita/ scrive solo l'utente";
# the agent never writes here. The writable @AGENT_DATA@ bind above already
# exposes this dir at .local/share/personalita/ inside the container; this
# line re-binds the SAME container path read-only. Created at S-73.
ro?  @AGENT_DATA@/personalita    @CONTAINER_HOME@/.local/share/personalita

# The active project. Everything read-only except the two write areas.
ro?  @PROJECT@                   @CONTAINER_HOME@/project
ro?  @PROJECT@/memoria.md        @CONTAINER_HOME@/project/memoria.md
rw?  @PROJECT@/proposte          @CONTAINER_HOME@/project/proposte
rw?  @PROJECT@/output            @CONTAINER_HOME@/project/output

# The note archive — read-only (§4.3). J3: "consultazione di un archivio di
# appunti personali, sola lettura". Path from PHI_AGENT_NOTES_DIR.
ro?  @NOTES@                     @CONTAINER_HOME@/notes
